      <Desc>WORLD MUSIC IN THE SCHOOLS, A UNIQUE PROGRAM PRESENTED BY THE CENTER FOR WORLD MUSIC, PROMOTES AWARENESS, SKILLS, AND KNOWLEDGE OF THE RICH PERFORMING ARTS TRADITIONS OF THE WORLD THROUGH WEEKLY HANDS-ON CLASSES AND PERIODIC STUDENT-INTERACTIVE ASSEMBLIES IN PRE-K12 SAN DIEGO AREA SCHOOLS. THIS PROGRAM REACHED OVER 10,000 STUDENTS THROUGH WEEKLY ARTIST RESIDENCIES, INTERACTIVE ASSEMBLIES, AND PRESENTATIONS OF VARIED MUSIC AND DANCE TRADITIONS IN SAN DIEGO AREA SCHOOLS AND ONLINE DISTANCE LEARNING. NEARLY 3,200 OF THESE STUDENTS RECEIVED SUSTAINED WEEKLY INSTRUCTION.MORE THAN 60% OF PARTICIPANTS ARE FROM LOW-INCOME, UNDERSERVED NEIGHBORHOODS. WORLD MUSIC IN THE SCHOOLS IS SUPPORTED BY THE NATIONAL ENDOWMENT FOR THE ARTS, THE CALIFORNIA ARTS COUNCIL, PTA, PTO, SCHOOL FOUNDATIONS, PRIVATE FOUNDATIONS, AND INDIVIDUAL DONORS.</Desc>
      <ProgSrvcAccomActy2Grp>
        <ExpenseAmt>19654</ExpenseAmt>
        <RevenueAmt>20235</RevenueAmt>
        <Desc>THE CENTER FOR WORLD MUSIC (CWM) HOSTED A PUBLIC CONCERT AND COMMUNITY WORKSHOP PROGRAM WITH YEAR-ROUND PERFORMANCES IN VARIOUS SAN DIEGO VENUES. ANNUALLY, CWM SHOWCASES 12 DIFFERENT WORLD MUSIC DANCE RADITIONS, ENGAGING AUDIENCES OF ALL AGES. THE TICKETED CONCERT SERIES FEATURES LOCAL AND VISITING ARTISTS, PROMOTING CULTURAL UNDERSTANDING THROUGH PERFORMANCES AND INTERACTION.FROM JANUARY TO JUNE, 2021, THE CWM PRESENTED SIX PUBLIC CONCERTS THAT ATTRACTED AN ESTIMATED 700 ATTENDEES.SEPARATELY, COMMUNITY PERORMANCES, IN COLLABORATION WITH LOCAL LIBRARIES AND CULTURAL GROUPS HIGHLIGHTED THE CITYS MUSICAL DIVERSITY. THE COMMUNITY PROGRAM INCLUDED FREE MINI-CONCERTS, WITH AN ESTIMATED 15 EVENTS THAT DREW OVER 350 PARTICIPANTS.SUPPORT FOR THIS INITIATIVE COMES FROM THE CITY OF SAN DIEGO COMMISSION FOR ARTS AND CULTURE, PRIVATE FOUNDATIONS, DONORS, AND TICKET SALES.</Desc>
      </ProgSrvcAccomActy2Grp>
      <ProgSrvcAccomActy3Grp>
        <ExpenseAmt>2810</ExpenseAmt>
        <RevenueAmt>51635</RevenueAmt>
        <Desc>THE CENTER RUNS A SCHOOL FOR TEACHING ODISSI DANCE (A CLASSICAL DANCE FORM FROM INDIA) TO COMMUNITY MEMBERS AS WELL AS TO STUDENTS IN PUBLIC SCHOOLS WITH MANY PUBLIC PERFORMANCES BY THE STUDENTS AND THE TEACHER. THE TEACHERS COME FROM INDIA ON P-3 VISAS TO BE TEACHERS IN RESIDENCE FOR A PERIOD OF ONE YEAR. THE CURRENT NUMBER OF STUDENTS IS 30 WITH TUITIONS VARYING FROM $20 TO $35 FOR ONE-HOUR CLASS.</Desc>
      </ProgSrvcAccomActy3Grp>
